# Accepted residual CVEs. Every entry documents why it is accepted and when to
# remove it. The Trivy gate in the release flow must pass with ONLY these
# suppressions -- a new finding means a new decision, not a new entry by reflex.
#
# SCOPE: this file is the complete app-image allowlist. The release gate builds
# the tts and render allowlists from reviewed static per-image membership before
# adding their image-specific files; it explicitly removes the app/tts-only
# libsndfile entry from the render allowlist.
# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck all retained entries: 2026-10-10.

# -- Debian trixie base (python:*-slim): no fixed package released yet.
# Remove each when `apt-get upgrade` in a rebuild clears it from the scan.

# Perl ships in the slim base; application code does not invoke it.
CVE-2026-9538

# curl / libcurl4t64 / libcurl3t64-gnutls (HIGH x3):
# system curl ships in base; backend Python httpx does not use system libcurl.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8927

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) (HIGH x1):
# terminal handling in base; Audicle runs headless in a container.
CVE-2025-69720

# libacl1 (HIGH x1): POSIX ACL library in base; no ACL operations in Audicle.
CVE-2026-54369

# libsndfile1 (HIGH x1): CVE-2026-37555 is an integer overflow in the IMA
# ADPCM WAV parser. Reference uploads accepted directly by Python's wave module
# are PCM; every other reference format and every chime upload is decoded by
# ffmpeg and stored as PCM before soundfile reads it. Bundled TTS chunks are also
# PCM. Audio from an explicitly configured remote TTS provider is decoded by the
# controlled ffmpeg subprocess to PCM16 before storage, ASR, caching, duration
# inspection, or soundfile, so provider bytes cannot reach the vulnerable IMA
# ADPCM parser. No Debian fix is available.
# Present in app and tts images; included here so the app scan (shared-only) passes.
CVE-2026-37555

# CVE-2026-8458 (curl/libcurl, HIGH): unauthorized connection reuse. No fixed
# package exists in Debian trixie as of 2026-08-10 (trivy status: affected,
# empty fixed-version). Present in all three images, which is why it lives in
# the shared file: each installs curl solely for the localhost container
# healthcheck; article fetching uses httpx, never libcurl. Re-check each
# release and drop this entry when deb13u ships a fixed curl.
CVE-2026-8458

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# CVE-2026-16742 affects systemd-homed record verification. None of the images
# runs systemd-homed. The four util-linux findings affect privileged mount and
# nsenter operations; the services run as nonroot with no capabilities and do
# not invoke those tools. Debian 13 has no fixed package versions for these IDs.
CVE-2026-16742
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# OpenSSL DTLS retransmission heap disclosure and denial of service.
# No fixed Trixie package is available.
# App and TTS use HTTP(S), not DTLS. Renderer egress blocks non-DNS UDP;
# its browser uses only the TCP proxy. Remove when Debian ships a fix.
# https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-84782
# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
CVE-2026-84782
